Validate scope for feature {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

ASSESS: Is this properly scoped as a feature or misclassified task?

READ:
(1) Feature description at {{.file_path}}
(2) Parent epic PRD for context

CRITERIA:
FEATURE = multi-capability (4+ user-facing capabilities), user journey focus (maps to persona needs), 4+ files typically, multi-sprint scope, requires architecture decisions.
TASK = single atomic change (e.g., 'update button', 'fix typo', 'change color'), implementation detail, 1-3 files, days of work, applies existing patterns.

IF MISCLASSIFIED:
(1) Find or create enhancement feature: shark feature list --title='Enhancements' --epic={{.epic_id}} OR shark feature create --epic={{.epic_id}} --title='Enhancements and Maintenance'
(2) Convert to task: shark task create --feature={enhancement_feature_id} --title='{{.title}}' --description='...'
(3) Cancel this feature: shark status set {{.id}} cancelled --note='Converted to task {task_id} under {enhancement_feature_id}'
(4) Report to user with task ID and feature ID

IF PROPERLY SCOPED:
(1) Add validation note: shark feature note {{.id}} 'Scope validated as feature: {reasoning}'
(2) {{template "advance" .}}

See docs/complexity-adaptive-workflow-proposal.md for full criteria.
